  <metadata>
    <name>Fairfield Horseshoe</name>
    <desc>17.5 km with 959 m of climb. From the Bracken Fell Harriers route book.</desc>
  </metadata>
  <trk>
    <name>Fairfield Horseshoe</name>
    <desc>The classic horseshoe over eight named tops: up by Nab Scar and Heron Pike, along the ridge to Fairfield's broad summit plateau, then back over Hart Crag, Dove Crag and the Pikes. This is serious mountain running — navigation gets genuinely hard on Fairfield's plateau in mist. Full fell kit, no exceptions.</desc>
